# Cargo / Rust build artifacts
# No trailing slash: since R1489 `target` is a SYMLINK onto the compressed
# build-cache volume, and `target/` matches directories only — the symlink
# slipped past it and got staged by `git add -A`. A machine-specific absolute
# path in a tracked tree would break every clone.
/target
**/*.rs.bk

# Vendored submodule build artifacts — submodule manages its own target/.
# Submodule itself is tracked (gitlink); only its build output is local.
vendor/sce/target/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# Mnemosyne — atomic store sidecar is the SSOT; commit it.
# .atomic/  ← do NOT ignore; it IS the source of truth post Round 251.
# (Mnemosyne R395–R400 retired the rendered docs/GENERATED.md view; humans
# read the store via `mnemosyne-cli query` instead.)

# Local Claude Code state — settings.local.json, transcripts, etc.
#
# The CONTENTS and not the directory: git cannot re-include a path inside an
# excluded directory, so `.claude/` + a negation silently keeps ignoring it.
.claude/*
# ...except what the REPOSITORY declares rather than what this checkout holds.
# `remote-build.toml` says which executables, system packages and resources a
# heavy build or test run needs, and which command verifies this tree. That is
# a property of the workspace, not of one machine's working copy: ignored, a
# fresh clone declares nothing and whoever runs it is back to guessing — the
# same shape `docs/SEED_PROMPT.md` being ignored already costs. It names no
# machine, address or account by construction; those live in the operator's
# own registry, outside any repository.
!.claude/remote-build.toml

# Claude-Specific Documentation per global CLAUDE.md convention —
# local working notes, ad-hoc analyses, and cross-project coordination
# drafts that should not enter pinion's git history. Historical entries
# that pre-dated this policy were untracked via `git rm --cached`; the
# working copies remain on disk so the prior context is not lost.
claudedocs/

# Activity logs (local working notes; outside mnemosyne workspace).
notes/

# Python bytecode cache emitted by the §5.49 R59 AI-first RPC
# self-verification harness when demos under tools/demos/ run.
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Session-local SEED prompt (untracked per dev request; lives on disk only)
docs/SEED_PROMPT.md
